# 🏭 FactoryMind: A Multi-Agent AI Manufacturing Factory

> **Where Six AI Agents Run a Factory, Together.**

An intelligent smart-factory simulation platform where six specialized AI agents — **Production, Quality, Maintenance, Inventory, Logistics, and Energy** — collaborate in real-time to autonomously manage and optimize an entire manufacturing ecosystem.

Powered by **Google Gemini API** for reasoning and decision-making, built with a **FastAPI (Python) backend** and a **React-based modern dashboard**.

---

## 📌 Table of Contents

- [Overview](#-overview)
- [The Six AI Agents](#-the-six-ai-agents)
- [Tech Stack](#-tech-stack)
- [Architecture](#-architecture)
- [Project Structure](#-project-structure)
- [Features](#-features)
- [Getting Started](#-getting-started)
- [Environment Variables](#-environment-variables)
- [API Endpoints](#-api-endpoints)
- [Screenshots](#-screenshots)
- [Future Scope](#-future-scope)
- [License](#-license)

---

## 🧠 Overview

**FactoryMind** is an AI-driven smart manufacturing platform that simulates a fully autonomous factory environment governed by a team of specialized, cooperating AI agents. Rather than relying on a single monolithic AI, the system distributes intelligence across **six domain-specific agents**, each responsible for one critical aspect of factory operations.

These agents continuously sense their environment, make decisions using **Google Gemini LLM**, and communicate with a central **Orchestrator Agent** to align on overall factory goals — mimicking how a human factory manager would coordinate departments, but running at machine speed.

> ⚠️ **Note:** This is a **practice/educational project** designed to demonstrate multi-agent AI coordination. It is **not intended for production deployment**.

---

## 🤖 The Six AI Agents

| # | Agent | Responsibility |
|---|-------|----------------|
| 1 | 🏭 **Production Agent** | Plans and schedules manufacturing orders, allocates machines, and optimizes throughput. |
| 2 | ✅ **Quality Agent** | Inspects output, detects defects, classifies product grades, and triggers rework decisions. |
| 3 | 🔧 **Maintenance Agent** | Monitors machine health, predicts breakdowns, and schedules preventive maintenance. |
| 4 | 📦 **Inventory Agent** | Tracks raw material stock, forecasts demand, and raises restock alerts before shortages. |
| 5 | 🚚 **Logistics Agent** | Manages shipment routing, delivery timelines, and coordinates dispatch schedules. |
| 6 | ⚡ **Energy Agent** | Analyzes power consumption across machines, detects anomalies, and reduces energy waste. |

### 🎯 Orchestrator Agent

All six agents are supervised by an **Orchestrator Agent** that:
- Feeds each agent with real-time factory context
- Collects decisions from each agent
- Resolves conflicts (e.g., maintenance vs. production priority)
- Produces a unified factory action plan per cycle

---

## 🛠 Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|------------|
| **Backend** | Python 3.10+, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, Uvicorn |
| **AI / LLM** | Google Gemini API (`gemini-1.5-flash`) |
| **Frontend** | React (Vite), Tailwind CSS, Framer Motion, Recharts |
| **Real-time** | WebSockets for live agent updates |
| **Database** | SQLite with raw SQL scripts |
| **Authentication** | JWT-based simple authentication |
| **Version Control** | Git + GitHub |

---

## 🏗 Architecture




---

## ✨ Features

- 🤖 **6 autonomous AI agents** with distinct roles and reasoning
- 🧠 **Orchestrator Agent** for multi-agent coordination and conflict resolution
- 📊 **Live factory dashboard** with KPIs, charts, and alerts
- ⚡ **Real-time agent activity feed** via WebSocket
- 🏭 **Visual factory floor simulation** showing machine states
- 📈 **Reports & analytics** for production, energy, and quality trends
- 🎨 **Modern dark-themed UI** with glassmorphism and neon accents
- 🔐 **JWT-based authentication**
- 🗄️ **SQLite database** with seed data

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

### Prerequisites

Make sure you have installed:
- **Python 3.10+** → [Download](https://www.python.org/downloads/)
- **Node.js 18+** → [Download](https://nodejs.org/)
- **Git** → [Download](https://git-scm.com/)
- **Google Gemini API Key** → [Get it here](https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey)

---

### 🔧 Backend Setup

```bash
# 1. Navigate to backend folder
cd backend

# 2. Create virtual environment
python -m venv venv

# 3. Activate virtual environment
# On Windows:
venv\Scripts\activate
# On Mac/Linux:
source venv/bin/activate

# 4. Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 5. Create .env file (see Environment Variables section)

# 6. Initialize database with seed data
python app/db/init_db.py

# 7. Run the backend server
python run.py


# 1. Navigate to frontend folder
cd frontend

# 2. Install dependencies
npm install

# 3. Create .env file (see Environment Variables section)

# 4. Run development server
npm run dev



